# Cursor & AI Agent Project Rules for NDHU Course Selector

## 1. Project Context
- This repository is the NDHU (National Dong Hwa University) Course Selector automation project.
- It is written in Python (>=3.11) using Playwright Sync API and managed via `uv`.
- Core application logic lives in `src/ndhu_course_selector/` using the standard `src-layout`.
- Root scripts `auto_login.py` and `main.py` MUST remain backward-compatible entrypoints.

## 2. Safety & Security Rules
- NEVER commit real credentials, student IDs, or passwords.
- Always read configurations via `ndhu_course_selector.tools.config`, which honors `.env` and `config.txt` (both git-ignored).
- When documenting or printing logs, always mask student numbers and passwords.

## 3. Automation & Latency Guidelines
- The browser must run in headed mode (`headless=False`, `channel="chrome"`) unless explicitly testing in headless mode.
- Preserve the two-tier latency architecture:
  - Query phase: stable delays (~150ms) to ensure ASP.NET postbacks and modals resolve properly.
  - Rush phase: ultra-fast human-like delays (20ms~50ms) for high-speed course clicking.
- Never introduce blocking sleeps or redundant waits during rush execution.

## 4. Documentation & Changelog Policy
- Any architectural change must be recorded in `DECISIONS.md` (ADR) and `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Keep `WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md` updated if the CLI prompts or user options change.
